# Lane-4a probe worlds ARE committed: a capability claim a third party cannot
# load and re-run is a self-attestation, which is what this lane exists to
# remove. They are generated by gen_worlds.py and checked by
# `gen_worlds.py --check`.
#
# Lane-4b's scaling worlds are NOT. They are parameterised by N, regenerated
# every sweep, and deleted at the end of a normal run -- but an interrupted
# sweep leaves them behind, and 20 near-identical rovers-at-N .wbt files are
# noise in a diff. They live in THIS directory (not a work dir) only because
# the engine resolves `controller "envelope_stepper"` relative to the world's
# project directory, so a world stored anywhere else cannot find lane4's
# controllers at all.
env_*.wbt
env_*.omniworld
